ing you will only improve you  won't get worse although it might seem  that you're better at sometimes than  others and it'll depend on how well you  connect with the people you're talking  to and a bunch of other factors how  comfortable you are in the environment  these or the  subject matter this will affect your you  know how comfortable how well you speak  but just keep doing it that's the first  thing the second thing is don't compare  don't compare yourself to others and I'm  gonna leave in the description box a  link to a video by a person whom I know  Christine she's French and she does  she's not a video in twelve languages  and she is spectacular  she is spectacular in languages as  different as Tamil and French and Korean  and Japanese and Russian Spanish and  Portuguese listen to this video and she  does it with humor and she it's a  phenomenal video and I can't compare  myself to Christine she's much better  than I am  that doesn't discourage me from learning  languages you know sometimes I did a  video with Luca Lumpur yalla and we  spoke can't remember which languages and  people say well look was much better  than Steve sure doesn't bother me the  fact that someone else is better than me  better pronunciation better use of words  for any number of reasons it could be  that they're simply more talented or  they have more opportunity or they went  to the country where the language is  spoken or for whatever reason it doesn't  matter people are not all going to  produce the language equally smoothly  well with equally native like  pronunciation you know close to the  native it doesn't matter don't compare  yourself also on the subject of of  humility if you look at christine's  video you'll see that she has like two  and a half million views which is  phenomenal  and she's got like 137 thousand likes  but she still got one point nine  thousand thumbs down I mean you watch  that video it's clever its witty she's  phenomenal in all these languages and  s